  "narrative": "The new validation results solidify the core dataset-specific main-effect cluster and close several original directions. For H33, the claim is that feature_037 lowers outcome_001 relative to its comparator. Discovery gave a signed effect of +0.833 (95% CI [0.767, 0.898]), and independent validation gave +0.798 (adjusted interval [0.697, 0.898]). Because the claim direction is negative, these signed positive values correspond to raw exposed-minus-comparator differences of approximately -0.80 to -0.83, i.e. feature_037-positive samples have more negative dependency scores and therefore stronger composite dependency. The entire validated interval remains far above the 0.15 claimed-direction threshold, so H33 is accepted and closed. For H84, the claim is that feature_010 raises outcome_001 relative to its comparator. Discovery gave +0.423 (CI [0.327, 0.520]) and validation gave +0.398 (adjusted CI [0.263, 0.534]); both entire intervals exceed 0.15 in the claimed positive direction. Thus feature_010-positive samples have higher, less negative dependency scores, corresponding to weaker composite dependency. H84 is accepted and closed. The same validation also confirms why original negative-direction claim H19 is unsupported: its signed estimates are negative because the raw contrast is positive, opposite to the claimed negative direction. H18 remains rejected: feature_024 level_001 versus level_002 had a tiny discovery signed effect and a validation estimate in the opposite direction, with intervals entirely or substantially below threshold. The supported findings are therefore not causal or generalizable associations but robust dataset-specific contrasts. The cluster is: feature_037 associated with stronger dependency (lower outcome_001), feature_002 associated with weaker dependency (higher outcome_001, already validated through H85), and feature_010 associated with weaker dependency (higher outcome_001, now independently validated). Negative findings remain broad: research-marker main effects and marker-signature interactions, overall feature_031, feature_031 signature subgroups, high-prevalence binary screens, several categorical contrasts, feature_024, and the original opposite-direction versions of feature_010 and feature_002 are rejected or threshold-excluded. The conditional contrasts show that the core feature_037, feature_002, and feature_010 associations persist across one another's strata and are not artifacts of a single subgroup; the feature_037-by-feature_002 interaction H86 was rejected. Main unresolved uncertainty remains the direct feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction H88: its discovery interaction estimate is +0.210 with CI [0.019, 0.400], and the component differences are suggestive but not interval-supported at threshold. The most informative next analysis is H106, the direct feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction restricted to feature_037=0, where the dominant feature_037 contrast is absent. This can determine whether H88 is a genuine modification pattern or a diluted/contextual pattern. The already registered low-log-PFS main-effect context tests for feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002 (H112/H114/H116) are the next best complementary context analyses. H88 should not be prioritized for validation unless H106 becomes threshold-level. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset only.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 synthesize: Core main effects now independently validated for the dataset-specific cluster. Accepted and closed: H33 feature_037 (raw contrast negative; stronger dependency), H84 feature_010 (raw positive; weaker dependency), and previously H85 feature_002 (raw positive; weaker dependency). Original opposite-direction claims H19 and H24 remain rejected. H18 feature_024 rejected/closed with validation. Accepted conditional contrasts H94-H110 and context contrasts H111/H115 indicate robustness across feature_037/002/010 strata and high-log-PFS context for feature_037 and feature_002; H113 high-PFS feature_010 remains unresolved due wide CI. Negative findings: markers/signature interactions, feature_031, feature_024, many binary/categorical screens. Unresolved: H88 direct feature_010 x feature_002 interaction, H106 feature_037=0 direct interaction (registered but unevaluated), H22 feature_003 overall borderline, low-PFS main effects H112/H114/H116, and H113. Priority next analysis: H106 plus H112/H114/H116. If H106 is subthreshold or imprecise, close/defer H88 interaction and return to untested predictors; if threshold-level, consider validation or stratum-specific refinement. Maintain dataset-specific association framing only."
}

