  "narrative": "These proposals sharpen interpretation of the validated dataset-specific cluster and resolve a few borderline follow-up questions. All returned estimates will already be signed to the claimed direction; for direction -1, a meaningful effect requires the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast to be more negative than -0.15 units, while for direction +1 it requires the raw contrast to exceed +0.15. First, I register a refined reference-cell test of feature_037 within samples that are negative for both feature_010 and feature_002. The double-absence tests for feature_010 and feature_002 are already covered by accepted H108 and H110, so I only add the feature_037 counterpart. If the feature_037 association remains threshold-level in this reference population, it strengthens the dataset-specific evidence that feature_037 is associated with stronger composite dependency, meaning lower outcome_001, rather than being solely carried by overlap with the feature_010 or feature_002 contrasts. If it falls below threshold, the original feature_037 contrast may be more collinear or context-dependent. Second, I register a low-log-PFS direct feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction as a complementary context test for borderline H88 and alongside already registered H106. H88 has a positive signed point estimate but an interval extending below threshold. If this low-PFS interaction is threshold-level, it would suggest the interaction is not merely diluted by the feature_037-restricted or overall context and would justify later validation; if not, H88 should probably remain deferred. Third, feature_003 is borderline in the original negative-raw direction: H22 gave signed +0.141, meaning raw lower outcome_001 with feature_003 present, but the interval does not establish a threshold-level effect. I propose three falsifiable decompositions: feature_003 in a population without the three accepted core labels feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002; feature_003 separately in high versus low log-PFS using the established feature_040 split at -5. These test whether the borderline signal is independent, concentrated by clinical context, diluted by context, or confounded by the core cluster. Finally, I add broad binary probes for feature_023 and feature_048 in the same core-label-negative population. These are exploratory independent-effect screens after removing the dominant feature_037 association and the accepted feature_010/feature_002 contrasts. Their directions are conservative negative-claim hypotheses and expectations are uncertain, but threshold-level results would indicate additional dataset-specific association patterns, whereas subthreshold or opposite results would keep the cluster interpretation parsimonious. No causal, mechanistic, or external-generalizability claims are implied; all proposed results would remain associations in this supplied dataset unless later independently validated.",
